From 9ff8b6209f1a231038d24ae22106e4be011e45cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:13:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 176/240] Bugfix: bound the renormalization factor when
 converting target part weights to integers [report R. Perry]

`_SCOTCH_METIS_doubleToInt()` and `_SCOTCH_ParMETIS_floatToInt()` look
for a common denominator of the floating-point target part weights.
For arbitrary weights, the renormalization factor grows beyond the
integer range within a few steps, so that the integer conversions
overflow and the resulting target weights are negative or null, which
makes `SCOTCH_archCmpltw()` fail.

The search now stops as soon as the factor would exceed 1e6, in which
case weights are rounded at that fixed resolution. Exact small ratios
are preserved as before.

Refs: CLI-08
